    T20
        title       Durability: restore, key versions and record migration (slice 2)
        status      draft
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@task.V3.T19]
        satisfies   [@plan.Inspection.O2, @plan.Persistence.O4, @plan.Persistence.O5, @plan.Runtime.O3]
        description
            Build restore and key versions from @spec.Restore and @spec.Codec, with record formats tagged from
            the first release.

            **Why now:** write-ahead records exist but nothing reads them back, so a reload cannot restore
            actors or deliver what was owed.

            **Read first:** @spec.Restore, @spec.Codec, @spec.WriteAhead,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/README.md (the `restore` row and the carry list).

            **Slice 2, durability (replan, accepted 2026-11-11), after @task.V3.T19:** absorbs @task.V3.T11 (the Restore
            area suite: oracles `restore` and `quarantine`, the migration wrong runtimes, C168 and the record-format
            carry rows) and @task.V3.T26 (record migration, @plan.Persistence.O5; real storage shapes are localStorage
            text now and IndexedDB structured clone in slice 9). Adds the Restore oracles, which re-judge every
            composite already built, record format tags, versions and resets, `forget` on the public route, and
            `previous` holds checked against Restore R6; the Restore and WriteAhead Specs gain the R2 KeyValueStore
            Invariant and a host store section. Codes: sr rl up fg pg. Part built: S25 [A]. Bench: the S25 upgrade boot.
            Read first: code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/replan-2026-11-11.md (part 3, "2 Durability").

            **Phase-out, step 5 (the user accepted 2026-11-11):** the Stamp twin (release 1 and 2 keys; `up`) is written
            in `fixtures/`; run the hand cases on each fixture on production; write production mutants per oracle the
            slice judges, mapped by Invariant from the round-14 mutants; delete the descriptor once the derived
            reference equals it (`stamp.ts` goes). Read
            code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/conformance-phase-out-2026-11-11.md.

            - **May change:** `src/`.
            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** restore read from memory, not bytes → caught by the restore oracle.
            - **Gates:** the suite; falsify.
            - **Stops:** a guarantee change.
        acceptance
            The Restore and Codec areas pass on production.
            - Every Restore Invariant has its oracle or case and each oracle kills its mutants (from @task.V3.T11).
            - Record migration passes cases on production: a changed saved shape resets its definition's records with
              the writes in flight kept (from @task.V3.T26, @plan.Persistence.O5).
            - The slice's generated runs pass on production, and its benchmark replay matches the work fingerprint.
            - Declared: sr rl up fg pg are in the production and Spec-model capability lists, and the feature-matrix
              gate shows none of them as owed.
            - Enabled: S25 [A] and the parts built earlier declare those codes among their needs, the generator draws
              their operations, and the app mix runs them.
            - Covered: the combination gate counts the pairs among implemented codes, fails an unexercised interacting
              pair with no dated waiver, and passes before this Task closes.
            - Guards: production's first-contact reds are recorded and classified, held-out seeds pass, and a sample of
              the model's expectations is read by a different model family (Fable).
            - Phase-out step 5: the Stamp twin exists in `fixtures/` and `stamp.ts` is deleted; the same verdict per
              case on round-14 and production.
            - Phase-out checks (the four validations): no lost catch in the catch matrix; the same coverage and
              feature-matrix rows; the derived reference equal to the hand rows wherever both exist;
              Compile static cases green on each fixture's `Compiled`.
        comment     2026-11-10T20:59:41Z
            Owns, in conformance/not-yet.ts, Codec I1 to I6 (round-14 has no canonical byte codec, Codec Q2). Their 
